From: Ferestre contributors
Subject: Harden token audiences in a bound service

The licensing audience a bound title may not take when the Player is the
Store account is now also any of the fixed licensing hosts:
licensing.xboxlive.com, licensing.mp.microsoft.com,
collections.mp.microsoft.com and inventory.xboxlive.com, compared by host
whatever the scheme, case, port, user info, path or trailing dot. Before,
only the audience the fetched endpoint list maps the licence service to was
refused, so a list that mapped it somewhere else, or could not be fetched,
left the gate open.

When the default endpoint list cannot be fetched, a bound service refuses a
title's XSTS request instead of using https://<host>/ of the request's URL
as the audience. The title can retry once the list is back. The service's
own licence path, which names a fixed URL, and an unbound service are
unchanged.

A service bound to a Store product but to no title identity refuses every
XSTS request that claims a title, from the title and from its own licence
path, and a licence request naming a title. Every launcher that binds a
product binds the title identity with it, so there is nothing such a claim
could be checked against. A request claiming no title is unchanged.

